  "problem_statement": "feat: run-completion notifications + cross-run daily spend cap\n\nScheduled runs happen unattended -- no way to know a run finished (or\nwent over budget) short of checking logs by hand. WELLS_NOTIFY fires a\ndesktop popup + Slack-compatible webhook on completion; WELLS_DAILY_BUDGET\ntracks cumulative spend in ~/.wells/spend.json and refuses to start a new\nrun once the day's cap is reached. Both off by default, wired into the\nheadless and TUI run paths, configurable via /config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
